                {
                  "content": "**Phone alerts** (devices as of Nov 6, 2026)\n\n| Push | Level | Devices |\n|:--|:--|:--|\n| New pairing you can take (pot or Tradeboard pickup) | Critical, buzzer | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| FLICA alert email | Critical | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| Hidden trip (seat open, gone from pot) | Critical | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| New charter / unusual A330 (CrewTrac) | Critical | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| Swap / add / drop request decided, with Pay-Gross | Time-sensitive | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| Swap idea | Time-sensitive | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| Drop ready (grid green) | Time-sensitive | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| Recall / Over 75 possible miss | Time-sensitive | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| Watcher stopped, needs you | Time-sensitive | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| H3628 LAX is up (Fanfare) | Time-sensitive | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone, MacBook (Hero) |\n| Watcher blind (no check 30 min) | Normal | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| App down 5 min | Normal | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| New ticket filed | Normal | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n| Ticket fixed, please check | Quiet (no sound) | iPhone 16, Ryan's iPhone |\n\n- **Apple Watch**: every push mirrors from the paired iPhone (Watch app > Notifications > Home Assistant > Mirror iPhone alerts). Critical needs Critical Alerts allowed for Home Assistant in iOS Settings.\n- **Not sent to**: iPhone 16 Pro (retired Nov 6), James's phone (his Watcher pushes only his own phone, and none of his reach yours).\n- Critical sounds through silent and Focus; time-sensitive breaks through Focus.\n- **Buzzer** (FW-0054): on each iPhone open /local/flight-watcher-buzzer.wav, save it to Files, then Home Assistant app > Settings > Companion App > Notifications > Sounds > Import. Until then the new-pairing push plays the default sound.\n- **Tickets**: Settings tab, bottom (Ryan only).\n\n**Health**: Hark checks every hour.\n\n**Rules editor**: Settings > Apps > Flight Watcher > Open Web UI.",
